    finding "W1" state="open" size="owed-work" \
        text="the engine wrote a record the record refuses. `bind`'s refusal carries `on-version`, \
            and the declared shape of `refusal` required `on-slice` and knew no such field. Two \
            refusal records were written and praxis check refused both" \
        note="every command before this wrote a conforming record because its shape was declared \
            FIRST and the writer built to it. Here the writer was built first and the shape \
            invented at the keyboard. The check caught it immediately, which is the system working \
            — but nothing catches it at the moment of writing, and a command that writes an \
            invalid record has already written it"

    finding "W2" state="open" size="observation" \
        text="there are now two write disciplines: compose-whole for machine-owned records, edit-in- \
            place for human-authored ones. The release index is entirely derived, so rewriting it \
            loses nothing; an iteration holds prose a person wrote, so a rewrite would" \
        note="the distinction is not about size or convenience — it is about who authored the \
            content. Worth stating as doctrine before a third command has to guess"

    finding "W3" state="open" size="owed-work" \
        text="the bump proposal had an input the record did not hold. config.kdl declares five bump \
            rules and nothing said which rule an iteration matched, so `contributes` was added and \
            seven closed iterations amended to carry it" \
        note="it is DECLARED rather than inferred on purpose. A diff cannot tell an added outcome \
            from a remediated gap, and a bump proposal inferred from one is a guess about intent \
            wearing the record's authority. But nothing refuses an iteration that declares none — \
            it is named in the release as incomplete, which is the softest enforcement in the frame"

    finding "W4" state="open" size="frame-sized" \
        text="the schema cannot say `exactly one of these fields`. A refusal is about a slice, an \
            iteration or a version, and on-slice/on-iteration/on-version are each 0..1 with no way \
            to constrain the choice ACROSS them. A refusal naming nothing at all is accepted today" \
        obliges="NA.260820.01/schema — a cross-field constraint, or a rule that carries one" \
        note="the first thing the record has needed to say that its own vocabulary cannot express. \
